{
  "slug": "qa-orchestra",
  "name": "Qa Orchestra",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "10 specialized QA agents for Claude Code. Each agent answers a specific question about your PR: Does this diff implement the acceptance criteria? What test scenarios do I need? Which existing tests will break? and writes a structured Markdown report to qa-output/ that you can paste into GitHub, Jira, or Linear. Stack-agnostic: works with any web application (React, Angular, Vue, Rails, Django, Spring Boot, etc.). Agents include: functional-reviewer (diff vs AC analysis), test-scenario-designer, smart-test-selector, bug-reporter, browser-validator (live validation via Chrome MCP), environment-manager, automation-writer (Playwright/Cypress/Selenium), release-analyzer (multi-repo diffs), manual-validator, and an orchestrator that chains them together.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **10 agents**.\n\n- **Agents** (10): `automation-writer` (Converts test scenarios into executable Playwright, Cypress, or Gherkin test code), `browser-validator` (Validates test scenarios against a running application using Chrome MCP — navigates, interacts, and verifies in a real…), `bug-reporter` (Use this agent when qa-output/functional-review.md or qa-output/browser-validation.md reports any gap, failed scenario, or blocked verdict), `environment-manager` (Checks out PR branches, runs setup commands, and starts the application locally for live testing), `functional-reviewer` (Compares code diff against acceptance criteria to find functional gaps, regression risks, and missing edge cases), `manual-validator` (Guides manual test execution scenario by scenario and produces a structured validation report), `orchestrator` (Routes QA tickets to the right agents in the right order — including environment setup and live browser…), `release-analyzer` (Analyzes a multi-repo release diff to map cross-repo impact, AC compliance, and deployment risks), and 2 more\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install qa-orchestra@claude-community` from `Anasss/qa-orchestra`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot"
  ],
  "pluginType": "wrapper",
  "wrapper": "agent",
